  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book reproduces the flags of the forty-five countries of sub-Saharan Africa together with the flag designed by Marcus Garvey in 1917 to represent an African homeland for Afro-Americans. A version of TICK-TOCK was originally created for gallery M, Harlem, New York City, 2001, in an attempt to counteract the silence on the subject of AIDS in New York City's Afro-American community" -- T.p. verso.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Under each flag, a digital clock counts down from 46 seconds to the moment before time's up. The french-fold pages are perforated to be broken open and to reveal AIDS statistics for each nation. Slip-covered in a translucent rubber cover, offset-printed.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 1000, with 30 signed and numbered copies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
